If you're a wizard, the game will warn you, and ask for you to confirm,
when you attempt an uncursed spellbook that has a chance of being too
difficult.

For any role, you can price-ID spellbooks to work out their level, and
from that you can calculate the chance of reading the book successfully
(as well as deciding whether it's worth buying/reading/blessing, if
there are only a few you're interested in).

As this chance depends on four variables, and you'd probably only
perform a few dozen readings in a complete game, building up enough data
to get a feel for this probability would take stupid lengths of time, so
anyone wishing to play unspoiled might be better with the conclusion you
drew above ;-)

